Provenance and upstream attribution
-----------------------------------

rusty-beagle is a derivative work of Beagle 5.5
(source release `beagle.250227` / `beagle.27Feb25.75f.jar`),
Copyright (C) 2014-2024 Brian L. Browning,
<https://faculty.washington.edu/browning/beagle/beagle.html>,
which is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
or (at your option) any later version.

Every module of rusty-beagle is a Rust translation of the corresponding
Java class or package of Beagle 5.5, rather than a verbatim copy: the
algorithms, parameter defaults, file formats and numeric behaviour are
those of the upstream program, re-expressed in Rust.  The per-file
headers name the upstream classes each file was ported from, and
`docs/PORT_NOTES.md` records the full source-to-source mapping,
including the places where the Rust code deviates from the Java.

In the terms of section 5(a) of the GNU General Public License, the
whole of this work is modified relative to Beagle 5.5: it was written
as a port during 2026 and carries prominent notices to that effect.

rusty-beagle is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or supported by the
authors of Beagle or the University of Washington.


Third-party dependencies
------------------------

rusty-beagle links the following third-party Rust crates (the full
dependency graph of `Cargo.lock`):

  flate2, zlib-rs, rayon, rayon-core,
  crossbeam-deque, crossbeam-epoch, crossbeam-utils, either

Each declares its own license terms in its own package (MIT OR
Apache-2.0 for all of the above except zlib-rs, which is under the Zlib
license); all are permissive and compatible with the GNU General Public
License version 3, so the combined work may be distributed under the
GPL.  These crates are neither included in nor covered by this
distribution; Cargo fetches them from <https://crates.io> and they
remain under their own terms.  To re-verify the declared licenses of
the exact versions pinned in `Cargo.lock`, run:

  cargo metadata --format-version 1 --locked \
    | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(p["name"], p["license"]) \
        for p in json.load(sys.stdin)["packages"]]'

Anyone redistributing a *binary* of rusty-beagle is distributing a work
that also contains those crates, and must satisfy both the GPL (for
this program: offer the corresponding source, see LICENSE section 6)
and the crates' own attribution requirements.
